3.text:
The EJR lower bound of 2 for voter 1 is settled by the quartet constraint (any committee intersecting A1 in 0 or 1 leaves voters 8–10 with fewer than 2 approvals each, and no other member of the quartet can compensate). The upper bound of 4 is realized by the explicit committee {x1, y1, z3, y4, y5}:

- size-6 x-group is satisfied (voter 1 receives exactly 3 approvals);
- size-4 y-group is satisfied (voters 4–7 each receive exactly 2 approvals);
- quartet is satisfied (voter 1 receives 3 approvals).

Symmetric swaps that keep exactly 3 seats inside U while preserving the same existential witnesses (e.g., {x2, y1, z3, y4, y6}) likewise meet every quota and still give voter 1 four approvals. No EJR clause forbids these fillings, and no valid filling can exceed 4 because only three seats are ever drawn from U. Hence the feasible range is exactly [2,4].

PUBLIC RESPONSE: A. min 2, max 4

